{{ 'commerce-showcase.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<section class="q-lab q-builder" aria-labelledby="Builder-{{ section.id }}">
  <header class="q-lab__header"><p class="q-lab__eyebrow">THEME EDITOR REFERENCE</p><h1 id="Builder-{{ section.id }}">Work with the theme files.</h1><div class="q-lab__intro rte"><p>Use this technical reference to find section names, setting IDs and accepted values. Work in a duplicate theme and review changes before publishing.</p></div></header>
  <div class="q-lab__guide-grid">
    <article><p class="q-lab__eyebrow">01 / CHOOSE</p><h2>Start with a world.</h2><p>Choose a preset in the theme editor, then assign the appropriate templates to your own products, collections and pages.</p><a href="{{ routes.root_url }}pages/features?view=documentation">Read the setup guide ↗</a></article>
    <article><p class="q-lab__eyebrow">02 / COMPOSE</p><h2>Use the real schema.</h2><p>Start with the compact section index. Read only the relevant section schemas through your theme-file connector; the full reference includes setting IDs, accepted options and block types.</p><a href="{{ 'quadratum-builder-index.json' | asset_url }}" download>Download the compact index ↗</a><br><a href="{{ 'quadratum-builder-manifest.json' | asset_url }}" download>Full schema reference ↗</a></article>
    <article><p class="q-lab__eyebrow">03 / REVIEW</p><h2>Keep people in control.</h2><p>Connect your own products, collections and content. Review changes in an unpublished theme, check the customer journey and approve publishing when your store is ready.</p><a href="{{ routes.root_url }}pages/features?view=documentation">Read the setup guide ↗</a></article>
  </div>
  <div class="q-builder__brief"><p class="q-lab__eyebrow">A USEFUL FIRST PROMPT</p><h2>Bring the brief. Keep your point of view.</h2><pre>Help me build a Quadratum store for [business and audience].
Start with [preset] and these products: [catalog].
I need [pages] with this visual direction: [brand details].
Read the compact section index, then only the schemas we need.
Use existing settings and blocks before proposing new code.
Work in an unpublished theme, preserve existing content,
and show me desktop and mobile previews before publishing.</pre><p>Review generated changes against your catalog, business requirements and customer journey.</p></div>
  <details class="q-lab__guide" open><summary>Product presentations</summary><div class="q-lab__guide-grid"><p><strong>Modern</strong><br><code>product.json</code><br>Gallery thumbnails and a flexible product summary.</p><p><strong>Classic</strong><br><code>product.classic.json</code><br>A familiar gallery and tabbed information.</p><p><strong>Image-led</strong><br><code>product.simple.json</code><br>A stacked photography presentation.</p><p><strong>Compact</strong><br><code>product.compact.json</code><br>A focused arrangement of buying essentials.</p></div><a href="{{ routes.root_url }}pages/features?view=products">Compare real products in every layout ↗</a></details>
  <details class="q-lab__guide"><summary>What a connected assistant needs</summary><p>A connector must explicitly provide access to theme files or theme settings. Catalog access alone does not grant editing access. This reference is a file inventory, not an installed app or an MCP server.</p><p>Give the assistant your business, audience, catalog, preferred preset and the pages you need. Ask it to use existing settings, preserve your content, work on an unpublished theme and show you the result before publishing.</p><p>Token usage depends on the model, connector and task. No token-saving benchmark is claimed.</p></details>
</section>
{% schema %}
{"name":"Builder reference","settings":[],"presets":[{"name":"Builder reference"}]}
{% endschema %}
